Recipe input routes (RFQ fill / LI.FI finalise / UniswapX execute)
├── when the initiating caller is unauthorized
│   └── it should revert before input is spent
├── when the callback sender is unauthorized
│   └── it should preserve the existing Reactor/settler authentication
└── when the caller and callback are authorized
    ├── when a native RFQ input total differs from the signed amount
    │   └── it should revert before transfers
    ├── when the RecipeExecutor has a zero/mismatched account or its connector is not version 2
    │   └── it should revert before the recipe transfer
    ├── when the recipe caller, commitment or managed action is invalid
    │   └── it should revert and roll back input, recipe effects and settlement state
    ├── when a route overdraws available LI.FI/UniswapX input
    │   └── it should revert and roll back the fill
    └── when recipe execution succeeds
        ├── with varying input amounts
        │   └── it should fund the connector, execute its account-only swap, and settle output
        ├── with mixed direct, discount and recipe routes
        │   └── it should execute each leg and settle their combined output
        ├── with multiple recipes
        │   └── it should fund each connector separately and return inventory to its bound account
        ├── with the upstream interpreter
        │   └── it should forward queries, steps, numeric inputs and proof-bearing runtime
        ├── when required output is missing
        │   └── it should revert and roll back input and nonce/claim state
        ├── with native output
        │   └── it should deliver through the existing settlement path
        ├── with post-calls in native RFQ
        │   └── it should run them after recipes and roll back on failure
        └── with LI.FI fees or retained LI.FI/UniswapX balances
            └── it should preserve the existing balance and settlement behavior
